1
00:00:30,199 --> 00:00:31,800
Ma Guowen deserved to die.

2
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:33,679
Liu Xuemei...

3
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,240
she had it coming too.

4
00:00:35,759 --> 00:00:36,719
What're you talking about?

5
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:37,439
What?

6
00:00:37,759 --> 00:00:38,799
If it weren't for her,

7
00:00:39,439 --> 00:00:41,200
would we all have ended up like this?

8
00:00:42,479 --> 00:00:44,079
If your life's a mess, who can you blame?

9
00:00:44,439 --> 00:00:45,119
Blame who?

10
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:46,759
Right.

11
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:47,840
I can't blame anyone.

12
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:48,719
What about Cao Jun?

13
00:00:50,159 --> 00:00:51,520
What about Cao Jun?

14
00:00:51,759 --> 00:00:53,119
Who did he ever cross?

15
00:00:53,799 --> 00:00:55,039
He was careful his whole life,

16
00:00:55,039 --> 00:00:56,240
scared of everything.

17
00:00:57,079 --> 00:00:58,679
Drove a forklift just fine,

18
00:00:58,759 --> 00:00:59,759
then sold tea eggs,

19
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:01,679
and then drove a three-wheeler.

20
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:03,920
Now he's been murdered.

21
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:05,519
And for what?

22
00:01:06,799 --> 00:01:08,079
Isn't it all because of that tramp?

23
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,400
That's enough.

24
00:01:09,959 --> 00:01:10,640
Qian Yichuan!

25
00:01:10,799 --> 00:01:11,519
They're already dead.

26
00:01:11,519 --> 00:01:12,560
Show some decency.

27
00:01:12,799 --> 00:01:13,640
If we can't talk about the dead,

28
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:14,760
Come on, have a drink. I'll talk about the living.

29
00:01:15,519 --> 00:01:16,000
What the hell?

30
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:18,079
What's the deal with your ex-wife?

31
00:01:18,319 --> 00:01:19,359
Why did she come back?

32
00:01:19,359 --> 00:01:20,799
To shoot a film for Ma Guowen?

33
00:01:21,079 --> 00:01:22,200
Is she on your side,

34
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:23,480
or on Ma Guowen's?

35
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:24,319
Back then— Are you ever gonna stop?

36
00:01:24,319 --> 00:01:25,799
Was she one of those who betrayed us?

37
00:01:26,159 --> 00:01:26,719
Just answer me.

38
00:01:26,799 --> 00:01:28,000
How much have you had to drink?

39
00:01:28,079 --> 00:01:29,760
Did she have anything to do with what happened?

40
00:01:29,799 --> 00:01:30,480
Qian Yichuan.

41
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:32,480
Watch your mouth.

42
00:01:32,719 --> 00:01:33,400
Talk sense.

43
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:35,599
Now that the brewery's gone,

44
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:36,560
and you have no job,

45
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:38,760
everyone understands.

46
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:40,840
Stop playing Mr. Nice Guy.

47
00:01:41,319 --> 00:01:42,599
What do you mean you understand?

48
00:01:43,719 --> 00:01:44,400
What?

49
00:01:45,079 --> 00:01:45,799
Like you had nothing to do with it?

50
00:01:46,439 --> 00:01:47,920
When pooling funds to buy the plant came up,

51
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:49,519
your eyes went wider than anyone's.

52
00:01:51,079 --> 00:01:52,159
The second the plan failed,

53
00:01:52,239 --> 00:01:53,840
you bared your teeth and turned on me.

54
00:01:54,879 --> 00:01:56,920
You took good care of your apprentices,

55
00:01:56,959 --> 00:01:57,640
but what about me?

56
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:00,560
Did anyone ever give a damn about me?

57
00:02:05,159 --> 00:02:05,879
Qian Yichuan.

58
00:02:08,879 --> 00:02:10,039
Some things are already in the past.

59
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:13,840
Ending up like this,

60
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:14,879
you've got no one else to blame.

61
00:02:16,759 --> 00:02:17,520
I'm not blaming anyone else.

62
00:02:19,919 --> 00:02:21,080
I'm a piece of trash.

63
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:22,560
A worthless life.

64
00:02:23,599 --> 00:02:24,680
A damn cripple.

65
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:28,479
But I'm not a bad person!

66
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:31,159
I didn't kill anyone!

67
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:35,280
Who said you killed anyone?

68
00:02:39,039 --> 00:02:40,520
Then what did you mean by that just now?

69
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:41,719
What did I say?

70
00:02:42,199 --> 00:02:42,759
Back up a bit.

71
00:02:42,759 --> 00:02:43,919
What did you say just now?

72
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:44,599
What did I say?

73
00:02:44,599 --> 00:02:45,520
Don't you shove me!

74
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:46,719
What did you mean by that earlier?

75
00:02:47,439 --> 00:02:48,520
You don't know what's good for you!

76
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:49,680
What are you doing?

77
00:02:50,039 --> 00:02:51,479
Don't point your fingers at my master!

78
00:02:51,479 --> 00:02:52,120
What's that supposed to mean?

79
00:02:52,199 --> 00:02:52,599
Tieping!

80
00:02:52,719 --> 00:02:53,360
What do you mean by that?

81
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,400
Don't wave your hands at my master!

82
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,439
You wanna kill me, is that it?

83
00:02:55,479 --> 00:02:55,960
Come on! Do it!

84
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:56,680
Tieping!

85
00:02:56,719 --> 00:02:57,280
Get out!

86
00:02:57,759 --> 00:02:58,360
Qian Yichuan, get out!

87
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,360
I'll kill this bastard!

88
00:03:00,439 --> 00:03:01,080
Get out of the way!

89
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:01,919
Move!

90
00:03:01,919 --> 00:03:02,400
Qian Yichuan!

91
00:03:02,439 --> 00:03:02,960
Get off me!

92
00:03:04,199 --> 00:03:04,639
Have you lost your mind?!

93
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:05,280
What?!

94
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,000
Beat me to death!

95
00:03:06,879 --> 00:03:07,280
Don't move!

96
00:03:07,319 --> 00:03:07,560
I...

97
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:08,080
Qian Yichuan!

98
00:03:08,639 --> 00:03:09,199
Let go!

99
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,280
If you've got the guts,

100
00:03:10,439 --> 00:03:11,280
hit me right here!

101
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:12,439
If beating me to death

102
00:03:12,439 --> 00:03:13,240
makes you feel better,

103
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:14,240
then go ahead and strike!

104
00:03:16,319 --> 00:03:17,800
Kill me today and you're a murderer!

105
00:03:18,159 --> 00:03:18,879
Go on, hit me!

106
00:03:18,919 --> 00:03:19,639
Look at you acting tough!

107
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:20,840
Get out of here!

108
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:22,159
What?!

109
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:22,639
Tieping!

110
00:03:22,639 --> 00:03:23,319
I'll slice your kidneys out!

111
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,000
Go! Move!

112
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:27,159
You're drunk!

113
00:03:27,199 --> 00:03:27,719
Get inside!

114
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:37,479
Sit down, sit down.

115
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:41,319
Sit down. Don't mind him.

116
00:03:41,719 --> 00:03:42,479
Psycho.

117
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,039
Come on, sit down.

118
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:47,879
Who does he think he is?

119
00:03:47,879 --> 00:03:48,360
Come on.

120
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:50,680
Tieping's had too much to drink.

121
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:51,840
Just sit.

122
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:57,840
The kid doesn't know any better.

123
00:04:02,919 --> 00:04:03,759
Look...

124
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:06,719
It's not Tieping's fault.

125
00:04:07,719 --> 00:04:08,680
I ruined the mood.

126
00:04:10,759 --> 00:04:11,599
Let me chug one.

127
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:12,879
Haipeng.

128
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:26,560
As for me,

129
00:04:27,279 --> 00:04:28,079
in a bit,

130
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:30,160
I'll go take a nap on the train tracks.

131
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:31,240
What do you think?

132
00:04:58,839 --> 00:04:59,639
Aren't you going to help him?

133
00:05:02,399 --> 00:05:03,600
None of my damn business.

134
00:05:04,759 --> 00:05:06,240
Let him sleep on the tracks forever.

135
00:05:07,319 --> 00:05:07,839
When a train comes,

136
00:05:07,839 --> 00:05:08,480
he'd better not get up.

137
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:09,439
Let it run him over.

138
00:05:15,399 --> 00:05:16,319
Originally,

139
00:05:17,399 --> 00:05:19,240
I wanted everyone

140
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,000
to get together

141
00:05:21,079 --> 00:05:22,040
and discuss

142
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:23,519
those two

143
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,360
murder cases.

144
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:26,480
But

145
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:27,439
who would've thought

146
00:05:28,519 --> 00:05:29,839
our own people

147
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:31,839
would start fighting each other.

148
00:05:33,399 --> 00:05:34,600
If we aren't united,

149
00:05:36,199 --> 00:05:37,759
nothing gets done.

150
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,240
Who do you think you're chopping at over there?

151
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:33,839
I'll kick things off.

152
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:37,480
Tomorrow is the day of the auction.

153
00:07:38,439 --> 00:07:39,560
These past few days,

154
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:41,160
those with money chipped in,

155
00:07:41,279 --> 00:07:42,279
and those with strength pitched in.

156
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:44,079
For our common goal,

157
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:45,399
we've all sacrificed a lot.

158
00:07:45,959 --> 00:07:47,199
We finally raised all the money.

159
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:47,759
Great!

160
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:49,560
Comrade Liu Xuemei

161
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,560
went to Qingzhou on our behalf

162
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:54,519
to handle the auction paperwork.

163
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:56,720
Great!

164
00:07:58,839 --> 00:08:01,040
As we welcome the new century,

165
00:08:01,319 --> 00:08:04,319
and a new chapter for our joint venture!

166
00:08:04,439 --> 00:08:06,160
Good, good, good!

167
00:08:06,439 --> 00:08:07,759
Hear, hear!

168
00:08:07,759 --> 00:08:08,720
Well said!

169
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:09,279
Engineer Chen.

170
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:11,560
Without Engineer Chen's leadership,

171
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:12,439
this whole thing...

172
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:13,560
would never have happened.

173
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,000
That's right!

174
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:14,439
Engineer Chen,

175
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:15,279
say a few words to everyone.

176
00:08:15,279 --> 00:08:15,839
Say a few words!

177
00:08:17,279 --> 00:08:19,319
Chief Engineer Chen, say a few words!

178
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:20,519
All right, I'll speak. Here goes.

179
00:08:20,959 --> 00:08:22,759
After tomorrow's auction,

180
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:24,360
we will become Lapi Brewery's

181
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:26,120
true partners!

182
00:08:26,279 --> 00:08:27,600
Great!

183
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:28,240
Hear, hear!

184
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,839
Let's all pull together

185
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:31,920
and make Lapi Brewery thrive!

186
00:08:32,159 --> 00:08:32,559
You bet!

187
00:08:32,559 --> 00:08:33,360
Great!

188
00:08:33,519 --> 00:08:35,279
As for me, on the technical side,

189
00:08:35,639 --> 00:08:37,320
I'll keep strict standards for us all.

190
00:08:38,399 --> 00:08:38,840
Come on!

191
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:41,799
Let's welcome the millennium together,

192
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,440
and welcome a new dawn for Lapi Brewery!

193
00:08:44,519 --> 00:08:46,279
Great!

194
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:48,360
Well...

195
00:08:49,039 --> 00:08:50,440
Let me say a few words.

196
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:51,879
You know,

197
00:08:52,159 --> 00:08:53,840
things are about to get better for us.

198
00:08:54,399 --> 00:08:55,440
Look at her, grinning from ear to ear!

199
00:08:55,879 --> 00:08:56,799
What I'm thinking is,

200
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:58,159
the Women's Federation hopes

201
00:08:58,399 --> 00:09:00,440
the brewery will provide better benefits

202
00:09:00,639 --> 00:09:01,799
for all our female comrades.

203
00:09:01,799 --> 00:09:02,799
Am I right, everyone?

204
00:09:02,879 --> 00:09:08,639
Absolutely! You bet!

205
00:09:09,159 --> 00:09:09,559
Yan,

206
00:09:09,639 --> 00:09:10,960
let's hear Qian Yichuan say a few words.

207
00:09:11,159 --> 00:09:11,440
Chuan'er, Chuan'er!

208
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:11,799
Say a few words.

209
00:09:11,799 --> 00:09:13,120
Yeah, tell us a few words!

210
00:09:15,399 --> 00:09:17,320
Then I... I'll say a few words.

211
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:18,960
I'm so excited today.

212
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:20,480
First,

213
00:09:20,879 --> 00:09:22,519
thank you to all the shareholders

214
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:24,600
for trusting us,

215
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,840
and for attending today's meeting.

216
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:31,960
A person...

217
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:34,279
I think we gotta have dreams.

218
00:09:35,399 --> 00:09:36,559
My dream is...

219
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:42,120
My dream is that one day,

220
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:44,360
people all across the world

221
00:09:44,639 --> 00:09:47,240
will get to drink our Lacheng beer!

222
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:48,679
Hear, hear!

223
00:09:48,679 --> 00:09:50,039
Great!

224
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:51,120
Once our...

225
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,360
brewery goes public,

226
00:09:54,799 --> 00:09:56,639
even private jets will be too slow for us.

227
00:09:57,279 --> 00:09:58,919
We'll be riding rockets everywhere!

228
00:09:59,159 --> 00:10:00,360
Awesome!

229
00:10:00,919 --> 00:10:02,039
Riding rockets!

230
00:10:02,639 --> 00:10:03,879
Alright, alright, alright!

231
00:10:04,159 --> 00:10:06,000
Then on behalf of the publicity department,

232
00:10:06,039 --> 00:10:06,879
I've gotta say a few words too.

233
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:07,799
Absolutely!

234
00:10:07,799 --> 00:10:08,320
Right?

235
00:10:08,519 --> 00:10:09,240
Today,

236
00:10:09,879 --> 00:10:10,840
this gathering of ours

237
00:10:10,879 --> 00:10:11,559
is just the prologue.

238
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:14,639
We gotta do this all the time, every year!

239
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,240
Right?

240
00:10:15,639 --> 00:10:18,440
Once tomorrow's auction is over,

241
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:19,320
we'll do something really big!

242
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:21,679
We'll drink cross-century style!

243
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:23,399
Great!

244
00:10:24,039 --> 00:10:24,559
Not done yet!

245
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,320
Not done, not done!

246
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,039
What else? Come on!

247
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:26,559
Chuan! Chuan! Chuan!

248
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:27,799
What? What's up?

249
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,039
Come on, come on.

250
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:29,720
What else?

251
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:30,679
Lately,

252
00:10:30,679 --> 00:10:32,080
inspiration's just been pouring out of me!

253
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:35,320
Following up on what Chuan said,

254
00:10:35,919 --> 00:10:39,240
I came up with a new slogan for our brewery!

255
00:10:39,399 --> 00:10:39,840
Listen up.

256
00:10:40,639 --> 00:10:41,639
Eight words:

257
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:44,039
Lacheng Beer,

258
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:46,279
Intoxicating the World!

259
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:48,120
Lacheng Beer,

260
00:10:48,159 --> 00:10:50,039
Intoxicating the World!

261
00:10:59,919 --> 00:11:03,559
The old Lacheng Brewery,

262
00:11:03,759 --> 00:11:07,279
Full of sunshine and hope,

263
00:11:07,639 --> 00:11:10,960
The aroma of our beer

264
00:11:11,039 --> 00:11:14,759
Drifting far and wide.

265
00:11:58,399 --> 00:11:59,600
There's definitely no problem with this.

266
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:00,840
We're having dumplings tonight.

267
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:01,679
Yeah!

268
00:12:01,679 --> 00:12:02,639
Who made these dumplings?

269
00:12:02,639 --> 00:12:03,240
For so many people?

270
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:04,320
Who made them? Did you?

271
00:12:04,679 --> 00:12:05,440
What's going on outside?

272
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:06,039
What's all this?

273
00:12:06,039 --> 00:12:06,759
What happened?

274
00:12:06,799 --> 00:12:07,399
What's going on?

275
00:12:07,399 --> 00:12:08,080
No idea.

276
00:12:08,559 --> 00:12:09,120
What's the deal?

277
00:12:09,279 --> 00:12:10,039
Why's the main gate locked?

278
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,120
Open up, will you?

279
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:11,639
Hold on.

280
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,000
What's going on here?

281
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,039
Listen up, all of you!

282
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:15,679
A thief broke into our plant!

283
00:12:15,799 --> 00:12:16,200
Say what?

284
00:12:16,279 --> 00:12:17,639
Every workshop, every department!

285
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:19,159
Right now, this instant,

286
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:20,919
get back inside and get screened!

287
00:12:21,159 --> 00:12:22,639
Don't loiter outside without a reason!

288
00:12:22,679 --> 00:12:24,159
What thief?

289
00:12:24,559 --> 00:12:24,960
Open the gate!

290
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:25,840
Open it up!

291
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,279
Cheng Youtian, what's your problem?

292
00:12:27,279 --> 00:12:28,279
Can't you understand me?

293
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:29,759
I said a thief broke into the factory!

294
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:31,440
A thief? Then go catch him!

295
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:32,120
Why the hell are you blocking us?

296
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:32,519
Exactly!

297
00:12:32,519 --> 00:12:34,039
Why block us? Right?

298
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:35,159
Where's the director?

299
00:12:35,879 --> 00:12:37,480
Does the director have to report to you?

300
00:12:38,519 --> 00:12:39,480
Let me tell you,

301
00:12:39,879 --> 00:12:41,480
I'm standing guard right here,

302
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:42,840
and let's see which of you gets out!

303
00:12:50,840 --> 00:12:51,399
So what now?

304
00:12:51,399 --> 00:12:52,519
We can't even go home?

305
00:13:01,639 --> 00:13:02,600
Over here! Come here!

306
00:13:02,679 --> 00:13:03,080
Hurry!

307
00:13:04,919 --> 00:13:05,639
What's this supposed to mean?

308
00:13:05,799 --> 00:13:06,519
What do we do now?

309
00:13:06,519 --> 00:13:07,159
We can't get out!

310
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,720
They're clearly blocking us in.

311
00:13:08,840 --> 00:13:09,799
It's—it's okay.

312
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:10,600
If we can't take this gate,

313
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:11,559
we'll just use another one.

314
00:13:11,919 --> 00:13:12,639
Head to the east gate!

315
00:13:12,759 --> 00:13:13,200
The east gate!

316
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:13,879
Tieping is back!

317
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:14,840
How is it?

318
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:15,440
Tieping!

319
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:16,159
Slow down, take a breath. How is it?

320
00:13:16,159 --> 00:13:16,960
What's the situation at the east gate?

321
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:18,320
Someone locked the east gate!

322
00:13:18,759 --> 00:13:19,080
The east gate?

323
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:19,600
East gate, the east gate...

324
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:20,320
Let's go, try the west gate!

325
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:21,000
Head to the west gate!

326
00:13:21,799 --> 00:13:22,240
The west gate!

327
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:23,519
Careful!

328
00:13:23,679 --> 00:13:24,559
The west—west gate?

329
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:25,480
It's surrounded by people!

330
00:13:25,639 --> 00:13:26,360
There's no way out!

331
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:27,360
Then let's climb the wall!

332
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:29,039
Climbing won't work either!

333
00:13:29,039 --> 00:13:30,320
There are people all along the wall,

334
00:13:30,399 --> 00:13:31,519
and they're holding clubs!

335
00:13:31,559 --> 00:13:32,080
Chief Engineer Chen is here!

336
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:33,000
Chief Engineer Chen!

337
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,039
Engineer Chen! Engineer Chen!

338
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:36,200
What's going on?

339
00:13:36,639 --> 00:13:38,840
Ma Guowen gathered a mob.

340
00:13:39,639 --> 00:13:41,519
Right outside the auction venue,

341
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,360
they're checking license plates!

342
00:13:43,679 --> 00:13:45,399
Any car with local plates,

343
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:47,080
they pull over and search.

344
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:48,120
What?

345
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:50,000
Wait,

346
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:50,720
then... then...

347
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,240
If local plates aren't allowed in,

348
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:53,840
out-of-town cars must be allowed, right?

349
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:54,639
I have no idea!

350
00:13:54,879 --> 00:13:55,799
What are you all huddled up for?

351
00:13:55,919 --> 00:13:56,639
Xuemei!

352
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:57,639
She's in Qingzhou!

353
00:13:57,759 --> 00:13:58,200
Right!

354
00:13:58,480 --> 00:13:59,919
She went to pay the deposit for us!

355
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:00,320
Exactly!

356
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:00,679
Let Xuemei go!

357
00:14:00,679 --> 00:14:01,679
Have Xuemei get a non-local car,

358
00:14:01,679 --> 00:14:02,360
and she can just go right in!

359
00:14:02,399 --> 00:14:02,720
That's right!

360
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:03,440
The problem is,

361
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:04,639
how do we contact Xuemei right now?

362
00:14:04,679 --> 00:14:05,159
How do we reach her? Listen to me!

363
00:14:05,159 --> 00:14:06,120
Listen to me! Listen!

364
00:14:06,639 --> 00:14:07,840
Xuemei and I made a deal.

365
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:09,360
As soon as she pays the deposit,

366
00:14:09,399 --> 00:14:10,639
she'll call me!

367
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:11,120
Then...

368
00:14:11,159 --> 00:14:12,399
Then what are you doing standing here?

369
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:13,759
Go wait by the phone, quick!

370
00:14:13,799 --> 00:14:14,480
Stay safe!

371
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:14,799
All right!

372
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:15,960
You guys stay safe too!

373
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:16,720
Go wait for the call!

374
00:14:19,159 --> 00:14:20,679
What—what are we gonna do?

375
00:14:27,159 --> 00:14:27,720
Head back!

376
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:35,759
To the venue!

377
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:36,639
Go to the venue!

378
00:14:37,039 --> 00:14:37,480
Get back!

379
00:15:02,399 --> 00:15:02,840
Boss.

380
00:15:02,879 --> 00:15:03,600
Can I make a call?

381
00:15:03,639 --> 00:15:04,159
Go ahead.

382
00:15:11,279 --> 00:15:11,720
Hello?

383
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:13,000
Hello, Chunyan.

384
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:13,759
It's me.

385
00:15:13,799 --> 00:15:14,600
It's Xuemei.

386
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:16,799
Deposit paid at Qingzhou's head office.

387
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:18,200
I got paddle number seven.

388
00:15:18,519 --> 00:15:19,559
Give my name and you can get in.

389
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:20,679
Xuemei.

390
00:15:20,879 --> 00:15:21,919
Things have gone bad here.

391
00:15:22,519 --> 00:15:23,600
Ma Guowen blocked

392
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:25,080
all the gates to our factory.

393
00:15:25,080 --> 00:15:26,120
None of us can get out.

394
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:28,120
I also heard the auction venue

395
00:15:28,279 --> 00:15:29,279
has been blocked off.

396
00:15:29,519 --> 00:15:30,360
Cars with local plates

397
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:31,360
can't get anywhere near it.

398
00:15:32,799 --> 00:15:33,519
Then what do we do?

399
00:15:33,879 --> 00:15:34,600
Director Chen said

400
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:36,639
you should take a cab from Qingzhou

401
00:15:37,039 --> 00:15:38,080
straight to the auction,

402
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:38,799
raise the paddle,

403
00:15:38,919 --> 00:15:39,759
and bid on our behalf.

404
00:15:39,799 --> 00:15:40,440
Hurry!

405
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:41,559
Okay.

406
00:15:41,919 --> 00:15:42,679
I'll head back right away.

407
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:45,919
Two yuan.

408
00:15:46,759 --> 00:15:47,320
How much?

409
00:15:47,879 --> 00:15:48,799
That was a long-distance call.

410
00:15:58,399 --> 00:15:58,840
Stop.

411
00:15:59,279 --> 00:16:00,120
Rewind it a bit.

412
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:02,919
South Sixth Street.

413
00:16:03,559 --> 00:16:04,840
Near the Lapi Brewery compound.

414
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:05,360
Yeah.

415
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:06,720
Do you have another angle?

416
00:16:07,279 --> 00:16:08,039
Look for one.

417
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:10,600
How about this?

418
00:16:19,799 --> 00:16:20,440
This person...

419
00:16:21,039 --> 00:16:21,879
Can you zoom in?

420
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:22,759
Sure.

421
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:29,360
Stop, stop, stop.

422
00:16:29,559 --> 00:16:29,840
Stop.

423
00:16:31,559 --> 00:16:32,120
Hold on a second.

424
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:44,440
After talking to you last time,

425
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:46,000
I secretly followed him.

426
00:16:46,559 --> 00:16:49,159
He went to the Lapi Brewery family dorms,

427
00:16:49,519 --> 00:16:50,639
right around our neighborhood.

428
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:52,000
He wandered around for a long time.

429
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:53,720
I pulled back so I wouldn't tip him off.

430
00:16:55,799 --> 00:16:56,960
Let me warn you once more:

431
00:16:57,480 --> 00:16:58,919
don't go acting on your own.

432
00:17:00,039 --> 00:17:01,480
He's a cop, after all.

433
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:03,399
He could easily be on a case.

434
00:17:04,359 --> 00:17:05,519
Cao Jun is in our compound.

435
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:07,200
The police will definitely look for clues.

436
00:17:08,839 --> 00:17:09,680
My classmate said that

437
00:17:09,680 --> 00:17:11,640
after Gao Xuelin graduated from the academy,

438
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:12,640
he was assigned to Qingzhou.

439
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,400
He applied several times

440
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:15,440
before he got transferred to Lacheng.

441
00:17:15,839 --> 00:17:17,119
Ordinarily,

442
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,599
Lacheng is smaller than Qingzhou.

443
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,400
People always want to climb higher,

444
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:21,319
yet he went the opposite way.

445
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:23,039
That's pretty unusual too.

446
00:17:24,559 --> 00:17:26,039
Did you find anything on his parents?

447
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:27,119
I did.

448
00:17:27,519 --> 00:17:28,799
It says both his parents are gone.

449
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:30,160
He's always lived with his grandma.

450
00:17:30,599 --> 00:17:31,640
His parents...

451
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:33,079
they're both dead.

452
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:35,279
Not sure what happened to them.

453
00:17:47,759 --> 00:17:48,359
Get out.

454
00:17:57,319 --> 00:17:57,920
Come in.

455
00:18:19,519 --> 00:18:20,279
Explain yourself.

456
00:18:23,799 --> 00:18:24,720
I was just wandering around.

457
00:18:25,559 --> 00:18:26,319
Wandering around?

458
00:18:26,799 --> 00:18:27,799
You were casing the place, weren't you?

459
00:18:29,599 --> 00:18:30,279
Xiao Gao.

460
00:18:31,359 --> 00:18:32,720
In the few days you've been here,

461
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:34,920
making up lies,

462
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:36,279
playing dumb,

463
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:37,200
wandering around...

464
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:39,240
That's your whole repertoire, isn't it?

465
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:40,480
No.

466
00:18:41,359 --> 00:18:42,119
Then what else do you have?

467
00:18:43,359 --> 00:18:44,359
Do you know what your job is?

468
00:18:45,319 --> 00:18:46,160
You're a cop.

469
00:18:47,039 --> 00:18:48,240
You're not a private eye.

470
00:18:48,559 --> 00:18:49,880
Are you working side gigs?

471
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:52,279
If you're taking side gigs, you'd better tell me.

472
00:18:52,759 --> 00:18:53,519
Let me tell you this.

473
00:18:54,880 --> 00:18:57,640
I don't care how you worked for Xu Qiang,

474
00:18:58,240 --> 00:19:00,640
but you're in the Lacheng CID now.

475
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:02,480
You're under my command now.

476
00:19:02,599 --> 00:19:04,119
If anything happens to you, I'm responsible.

477
00:19:04,119 --> 00:19:04,839
You get that?

478
00:19:09,319 --> 00:19:11,079
I just wanted to look into Liu Xuemei's case.

479
00:19:13,759 --> 00:19:14,759
I think it's connected to Cao Jun

480
00:19:14,759 --> 00:19:16,400
and Ma Guowen's cases.

481
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:21,480
I just want to know how she actually died back then.

482
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:23,039
What happened before she died?

483
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:24,480
Froze to death.

484
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:27,119
Why can't you just let this go?

485
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:31,240
Fine, I'll tell you one last time.

486
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:32,200
Listen carefully.

487
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:34,319
Liu Xuemei

488
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:35,599
froze to death back then.

489
00:19:36,160 --> 00:19:37,720
Alcohol was found in her system.

490
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:38,640
So,

491
00:19:38,759 --> 00:19:40,519
she suffered hypothermia while drunk

492
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:41,240
and froze to death.

493
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:42,319
She...

494
00:19:42,319 --> 00:19:43,440
A beer taster isn't allowed to drink.

495
00:19:44,079 --> 00:19:45,319
How could she have been drunk?

496
00:19:47,319 --> 00:19:48,599
Beer tasters aren't supposed to drink,

497
00:19:49,359 --> 00:19:50,200
but she did.

498
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:50,960
So what?

499
00:19:51,359 --> 00:19:52,799
Then why didn't she go home afterward?

500
00:19:53,079 --> 00:19:54,079
Just sitting outside,

501
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:55,720
sitting there on Millennium Eve?

502
00:19:56,559 --> 00:19:57,559
It was Millennium Eve.

503
00:19:57,720 --> 00:19:58,599
She was celebrating.

504
00:19:58,680 --> 00:19:59,680
Celebrating alone?

505
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:01,440
Where were the people celebrating with her?

506
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:02,319
Where did they go?

507
00:20:03,039 --> 00:20:04,480
She was celebrating by herself.

508
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:05,240
What of it?

509
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:08,319
Celebrating alone by a bench,

510
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:09,559
sitting there all night?

511
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:11,799
Were there any empty bottles around her?

512
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:13,200
Didn't she drink?

513
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:22,799
Xiao Gao,

514
00:20:24,759 --> 00:20:25,799
you're a sharp kid.

515
00:20:26,519 --> 00:20:27,119
Quick on your feet,

516
00:20:27,880 --> 00:20:28,559
inquisitive,

517
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:30,200
always asking questions.

518
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:31,799
But remember this:

519
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:34,720
when you question me,

520
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:36,039
fix your attitude, all right?

521
00:20:38,599 --> 00:20:39,279
And another thing,

522
00:20:40,279 --> 00:20:41,480
pulling you out here

523
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:42,240
to talk in private

524
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:43,400
was to save your face.

525
00:20:44,319 --> 00:20:45,799
Next time, no more acting on your own.

526
00:20:46,039 --> 00:20:47,759
If I catch you going rogue again,

527
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,039
I'll send you back where you came from.

528
00:20:49,119 --> 00:20:49,880
Understood?

529
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:51,559
Understood.

530
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:52,920
Louder!

531
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:53,599
Understood!

532
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:00,920
It's good to think.

533
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:03,000
Keep thinking, then.

534
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:09,079
Am I supposed to think out here?

535
00:21:12,319 --> 00:21:13,279
Aren't you afraid of freezing to death?

536
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:15,559
I am, I am, I am!

537
00:21:27,079 --> 00:21:27,640
What are you looking at?

538
00:21:35,119 --> 00:21:36,279
Wearing a chamber pot on your head late at night,

539
00:21:36,279 --> 00:21:37,440
what are you wandering around for?

540
00:21:40,559 --> 00:21:41,319
Looking like a total dumbass.

541
00:21:55,359 --> 00:21:55,880
Pedal faster!

542
00:22:55,319 --> 00:22:55,759
Captain Han.

543
00:22:56,799 --> 00:22:57,440
How is he?

544
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:58,720
He's still breathing.

545
00:22:59,240 --> 00:22:59,880
He's still breathing.

546
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:02,759
Isn't that Old Qian from the gate?

547
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:04,039
Xiao Wu.

548
00:23:04,279 --> 00:23:05,039
Go with them.

549
00:23:05,039 --> 00:23:05,839
Do everything to save him!

550
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:06,440
Got it, will do!

551
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:07,640
Let me know the second there's any update.

552
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:08,119
Right.

553
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:12,799
Are there any cameras nearby?

554
00:23:12,920 --> 00:23:13,759
It's too remote out here.

555
00:23:14,759 --> 00:23:15,279
None at all.

556
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:17,200
Put up police tape right now.

557
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:20,559
Check all suspicious people and vehicles.

558
00:23:21,160 --> 00:23:22,480
Look for eyewitnesses.

559
00:23:23,240 --> 00:23:24,440
Take photos and collect evidence.

560
00:23:24,519 --> 00:23:24,920
Yes, sir!

561
00:23:47,640 --> 00:23:48,119
Xiao Gao,

562
00:23:48,519 --> 00:23:49,559
I'm going to the bathroom.

563
00:23:49,920 --> 00:23:51,480
Wait for me by that convenience store.

564
00:23:51,599 --> 00:23:52,720
I'll be right back.

565
00:24:14,720 --> 00:24:15,400
Where do you think you're going?

566
00:24:15,880 --> 00:24:16,839
I'm talking to you!

567
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:18,279
Freeze!

568
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:20,759
Stop right there!

569
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:22,920
Don't move!

570
00:24:26,319 --> 00:24:26,920
Don't run!

571
00:24:36,319 --> 00:24:36,960
Where's Xiao Gao?

572
00:24:38,119 --> 00:24:38,799
Gao Xuelin!

573
00:24:39,279 --> 00:24:39,880
Gao Xuelin!

574
00:25:06,279 --> 00:25:07,240
Last night,

575
00:25:07,880 --> 00:25:08,960
what happened with you?

576
00:25:09,359 --> 00:25:10,359
Here's the thing, Captain Cheng.

577
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:12,240
Last night,

578
00:25:13,279 --> 00:25:15,599
I stayed with my partner Cai Wenxiu.

579
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:18,640
We were at the brewery compound,

580
00:25:19,279 --> 00:25:20,519
staking out downstairs

581
00:25:20,519 --> 00:25:21,839
to see if we could find any leads.

582
00:25:22,359 --> 00:25:23,599
Just for a brief moment,

583
00:25:23,720 --> 00:25:24,920
Sister Cai said she had to use the restroom,

584
00:25:25,079 --> 00:25:25,519
right?

585
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:26,960
She told me to wait for her there.

586
00:25:27,960 --> 00:25:29,200
Coincidentally,

587
00:25:29,240 --> 00:25:30,359
right around that time,

588
00:25:30,759 --> 00:25:32,000
just as Sister Cai walked away,

589
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:34,440
a guy came out of Shen Leshui's building.

590
00:25:34,720 --> 00:25:35,640
He was bundled up tight,

591
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:36,799
so I couldn't see his face clearly.

592
00:25:36,839 --> 00:25:38,079
I called out, "What are you doing?"

593
00:25:38,519 --> 00:25:39,720
He took one look at me

594
00:25:40,079 --> 00:25:41,359
and turned and ran.

595
00:25:41,720 --> 00:25:43,000
So I chased after him the whole way.

596
00:25:43,160 --> 00:25:43,680
That's how

597
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:44,759
the two of us got separated.

598
00:25:46,359 --> 00:25:48,079
Then why didn't you call Xiao Cai

599
00:25:48,799 --> 00:25:49,559
and notify the team?

600
00:25:49,759 --> 00:25:50,680
I was in hot pursuit,

601
00:25:50,680 --> 00:25:51,799
so I didn't have time!

602
00:25:52,319 --> 00:25:53,359
While I was chasing him,

603
00:25:53,359 --> 00:25:54,960
Sister Cai called me.

604
00:25:55,160 --> 00:25:56,839
In the snow, my hand slipped,

605
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:58,279
and my phone hit the ground.

606
00:25:58,359 --> 00:26:00,319
By the time I looked up, he was gone.

607
00:26:00,519 --> 00:26:01,880
But I got some leads on the guy.

608
00:26:01,920 --> 00:26:04,279
He's between 180 and 185 centimeters tall,

609
00:26:05,319 --> 00:26:06,079
hard to tell his build,

610
00:26:06,079 --> 00:26:07,160
wearing a black padded jacket.

611
00:26:07,279 --> 00:26:08,359
He ran very fast,

612
00:26:08,559 --> 00:26:10,799
so he's definitely not older.

613
00:26:11,440 --> 00:26:12,119
Xiao Gao.

614
00:26:13,079 --> 00:26:14,000
Lately,

615
00:26:14,319 --> 00:26:15,640
you seem a bit too fixated

616
00:26:16,160 --> 00:26:17,359
on this Shen Leshui.

617
00:26:23,359 --> 00:26:24,480
What do you mean, Captain Cheng?

618
00:26:25,640 --> 00:26:27,279
Shen Leshui received a threat letter!

619
00:26:27,359 --> 00:26:28,279
As a detective,

620
00:26:28,279 --> 00:26:29,240
facing a situation like that,

621
00:26:29,279 --> 00:26:30,160
was I not supposed to chase him?

622
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:32,400
Just wait for my partner to finish in the restroom?

623
00:26:32,440 --> 00:26:34,119
Why didn't you call Xiao Cai?

624
00:26:34,359 --> 00:26:35,079
Why didn't you notify the team?

625
00:26:35,759 --> 00:26:36,839
My phone broke!

626
00:26:36,839 --> 00:26:37,400
Look,

627
00:26:37,400 --> 00:26:38,920
it was smashed to pieces.

628
00:26:39,480 --> 00:26:41,279
And after I lost the guy,

629
00:26:41,480 --> 00:26:43,200
I searched the area for at least

630
00:26:43,200 --> 00:26:44,480
two to three hours.

631
00:26:45,119 --> 00:26:46,480
I think you were so eager for credit

632
00:26:46,920 --> 00:26:47,880
that you lost your cool.

633
00:26:48,960 --> 00:26:49,799
No, that's not it!

634
00:26:50,039 --> 00:26:51,319
It was all just a coincidence.

635
00:26:51,319 --> 00:26:52,960
If I hadn't taken that call,

636
00:26:53,039 --> 00:26:54,200
my phone wouldn't have broken.

637
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:55,480
I would've reported to the team,

638
00:26:55,640 --> 00:26:57,079
and I definitely would've caught him!

639
00:26:57,079 --> 00:26:57,920
After all that talk,

640
00:26:58,039 --> 00:26:59,119
it's all someone else's fault.

641
00:26:59,319 --> 00:27:00,359
You're not to blame at all, right?

642
00:27:00,480 --> 00:27:01,240
Is that what you're saying?

643
00:27:01,319 --> 00:27:02,440
Well, I'm really confused.

644
00:27:02,440 --> 00:27:02,920
Captain,

645
00:27:03,039 --> 00:27:03,640
you've got to tell me

646
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:04,640
what I did wrong.

647
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:05,599
In my duties,

648
00:27:05,720 --> 00:27:07,160
where did I mess up?

649
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:09,400
Get out.

650
00:27:09,920 --> 00:27:10,599
Cool off.

651
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:14,039
He's your trainee.

652
00:27:14,160 --> 00:27:15,119
Teach him properly.

653
00:27:15,279 --> 00:27:16,119
Get out!

654
00:27:30,839 --> 00:27:31,559
Captain Cheng,

655
00:27:32,559 --> 00:27:33,920
I'll contact

656
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:35,000
the local police station right away,

657
00:27:35,319 --> 00:27:36,319
pull up all the surveillance footage,

658
00:27:36,680 --> 00:27:38,440
and check the guy Gao Xuelin mentioned.

659
00:27:38,680 --> 00:27:40,279
Until this case is cleared up,

660
00:27:40,559 --> 00:27:41,480
suspend him from duty.

661
00:27:42,519 --> 00:27:43,319
Don't be mad.

662
00:27:43,799 --> 00:27:44,640
He's young.

663
00:27:45,759 --> 00:27:46,799
Nothing to get upset over.

664
00:27:46,960 --> 00:27:48,000
Passion is a good thing.

665
00:27:48,559 --> 00:27:49,359
Just guide him more.

666
00:27:50,079 --> 00:27:51,079
I have a meeting at the bureau.

667
00:27:51,319 --> 00:27:51,640
Okay.

668
00:27:51,720 --> 00:27:52,240
I'll head over first.

669
00:27:52,519 --> 00:27:53,279
If anything comes up,

670
00:27:53,599 --> 00:27:54,400
keep me posted, okay?

671
00:27:55,119 --> 00:27:56,079
All right, carry on.

672
00:27:56,519 --> 00:27:56,839
Get back to work.

673
00:28:00,119 --> 00:28:00,799
Wu,

674
00:28:02,039 --> 00:28:03,480
contact the local station

675
00:28:04,039 --> 00:28:04,839
and get the footage.

676
00:28:05,279 --> 00:28:06,160
Chuang, about that...

677
00:28:06,279 --> 00:28:07,559
I already reached out to the station.

678
00:28:07,680 --> 00:28:08,440
The footage will be here soon.

679
00:28:09,079 --> 00:28:09,799
Pretty sharp.

680
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:15,480
Hello?

681
00:28:18,119 --> 00:28:18,519
Okay.

682
00:28:18,519 --> 00:28:19,880
I... I'll head over right now.

683
00:28:21,880 --> 00:28:23,279
Shen Leshui's place was broken into.

684
00:28:24,559 --> 00:28:25,640
You two, come with me.

685
00:28:26,240 --> 00:28:26,640
Sure.

686
00:28:35,839 --> 00:28:36,279
Chuang.

687
00:28:37,559 --> 00:28:38,359
Where are you guys going?

688
00:28:40,759 --> 00:28:42,319
Shen Leshui's place was burgled.

689
00:28:43,720 --> 00:28:44,880
Let me come along with you.

690
00:28:46,519 --> 00:28:47,519
You stay at the station.

691
00:28:47,839 --> 00:28:49,079
Until a decision comes down,

692
00:28:49,079 --> 00:28:49,880
don't go anywhere.

693
00:28:51,119 --> 00:28:51,680
Wu,

694
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:53,119
you're not coming with us either.

695
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:54,880
Keep an eye on him.

696
00:28:55,119 --> 00:28:55,680
Got it.

697
00:28:58,799 --> 00:28:59,839
Chuang, I need to talk to you.

698
00:29:01,920 --> 00:29:03,000
Can you spare a minute?

699
00:29:03,400 --> 00:29:04,319
It's really important.

700
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:14,839
Go downstairs and start the car.

701
00:29:19,880 --> 00:29:20,440
Go ahead.

702
00:29:26,480 --> 00:29:27,359
Chuang, I know

703
00:29:28,759 --> 00:29:30,559
you've never really trusted me.

704
00:29:32,359 --> 00:29:33,759
Of course, that's on me.

705
00:29:36,480 --> 00:29:38,200
After thinking it over today,

706
00:29:39,279 --> 00:29:40,759
there's something I must tell you.

707
00:30:05,599 --> 00:30:06,720
When did you realize they were gone?

708
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:08,000
Last night.

709
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:09,720
When I got back from a friend's place,

710
00:30:09,839 --> 00:30:10,839
I found the lock had been picked.

711
00:30:11,480 --> 00:30:12,200
What was stolen?

712
00:30:12,960 --> 00:30:13,519
Tapes.

713
00:30:14,160 --> 00:30:14,880
Only the tapes?

714
00:30:15,720 --> 00:30:16,400
Where were they kept?

715
00:30:16,799 --> 00:30:17,599
Over by the desk.

716
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:25,799
Aren't these still here?

717
00:30:26,160 --> 00:30:26,920
Not these.

718
00:30:27,359 --> 00:30:29,359
All unused Malt Kingdom footage is gone.

719
00:30:29,960 --> 00:30:30,519
How many tapes?

720
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:32,200
A shoebox with 13 tapes.

721
00:30:32,720 --> 00:30:33,279
All gone.

722
00:30:37,839 --> 00:30:40,079
The ones Xiao Gao wanted to see last time, right?

723
00:30:40,960 --> 00:30:41,519
Yes.

724
00:30:42,720 --> 00:30:43,480
Why isn't he here?

725
00:30:44,839 --> 00:30:45,640
He's on another assignment.

726
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:48,839
Well...

727
00:30:49,039 --> 00:30:50,200
Do you have a backup of the footage?

728
00:30:51,480 --> 00:30:52,799
I was just about to back it up.

729
00:30:52,960 --> 00:30:54,200
Didn't expect the thief to strike so fast.

730
00:30:59,400 --> 00:31:01,079
Only the unused footage was stolen?

731
00:31:02,799 --> 00:31:03,359
Yes.

732
00:31:30,519 --> 00:31:31,079
What?

733
00:31:31,359 --> 00:31:32,319
Caught a cold?

734
00:31:33,079 --> 00:31:34,200
Go out in just a thin shirt

735
00:31:34,359 --> 00:31:36,079
and take a stroll, see what happens.

736
00:31:40,680 --> 00:31:41,759
That's a pretty deep cough.

737
00:31:42,920 --> 00:31:43,960
You pissed me off so bad I'm wheezing.

738
00:31:44,799 --> 00:31:45,359
If it doesn't get better soon,

739
00:31:45,400 --> 00:31:46,640
I'll have the nurse give you some meds.

740
00:31:47,319 --> 00:31:48,079
Put it on my tab.

741
00:31:48,759 --> 00:31:49,319
What?

742
00:31:49,319 --> 00:31:50,079
Your treat?

743
00:31:51,319 --> 00:31:52,319
My treat, of course.

744
00:31:55,559 --> 00:31:56,359
Does it hurt?

745
00:31:57,119 --> 00:31:58,559
What's the filling?

746
00:32:00,759 --> 00:32:01,799
Pickled cabbage.

747
00:32:02,160 --> 00:32:03,240
Did you put pork cracklings in?

748
00:32:04,799 --> 00:32:05,359
Sure did.

749
00:32:06,240 --> 00:32:07,160
Hurry up and let me taste one.

750
00:32:07,160 --> 00:32:08,240
They'll get cold soon.

751
00:32:09,319 --> 00:32:09,960
You're clutching my hand.

752
00:32:09,960 --> 00:32:10,880
How am I supposed to grab them?

753
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:18,720
Look at you.

754
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:23,480
Here.

755
00:32:26,680 --> 00:32:27,240
Hot!

756
00:32:27,559 --> 00:32:28,200
Still piping hot. Careful, slow down.

757
00:32:30,319 --> 00:32:31,559
Did you get a good look?

758
00:32:32,319 --> 00:32:33,359
Who beat you up?

759
00:32:33,519 --> 00:32:34,200
Didn't see clearly.

760
00:32:35,400 --> 00:32:36,079
Pitch-black out,

761
00:32:36,400 --> 00:32:37,319
pitch-black guy.

762
00:32:37,960 --> 00:32:39,240
An assassin from Africa?

763
00:32:39,920 --> 00:32:40,960
An international hit job?

764
00:32:45,839 --> 00:32:46,960
Who the hell was it?

765
00:32:47,839 --> 00:32:48,880
If I ever catch him,

766
00:32:49,319 --> 00:32:50,240
I'll rip his hip right off.

767
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:54,000
What're you laughing at?

768
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:54,759
You knucklehead.

769
00:32:58,160 --> 00:32:58,839
Let me tell you,

770
00:32:59,799 --> 00:33:00,920
dying is really no big deal.

771
00:33:02,880 --> 00:33:03,839
The only thing I'd miss

772
00:33:03,839 --> 00:33:04,920
is your pickled cabbage dumplings.

773
00:33:06,400 --> 00:33:07,359
Even that won't shut your mouth.

774
00:33:09,359 --> 00:33:10,119
They're really good.

775
00:33:10,680 --> 00:33:11,400
Gimme another one.

776
00:33:11,920 --> 00:33:13,079
Think I'm a piggy bank?

777
00:33:14,440 --> 00:33:15,079
I'm choking!

778
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:15,920
Get me some water!

779
00:33:40,839 --> 00:33:41,440
What are you doing?

780
00:33:43,559 --> 00:33:44,519
Paying your last respects?

781
00:33:53,759 --> 00:33:55,680
Why do you three have chamber pots on your heads too?

782
00:33:57,799 --> 00:33:58,680
Not dead.

783
00:34:03,920 --> 00:34:04,759
Didn't die.

784
00:34:06,720 --> 00:34:07,680
Did you see who did it?

785
00:34:08,079 --> 00:34:08,679
I saw him.

786
00:34:09,760 --> 00:34:10,480
Someone I know.

787
00:34:12,440 --> 00:34:13,320
Someone you know?

788
00:34:14,480 --> 00:34:15,079
Who was it?

789
00:34:26,800 --> 00:34:27,559
Cao Jun!

790
00:34:30,480 --> 00:34:32,000
Are you crazy?

791
00:34:32,639 --> 00:34:33,760
I'll beat the crap out of you!

792
00:34:36,960 --> 00:34:37,480
Serves you right.

793
00:34:37,880 --> 00:34:38,480
It really hurts.

794
00:34:39,320 --> 00:34:40,079
Hey, we came

795
00:34:40,880 --> 00:34:42,599
all this way to see you,

796
00:34:43,360 --> 00:34:44,519
and my car even broke down.

797
00:34:45,119 --> 00:34:46,159
We had to take Tieping's

798
00:34:46,679 --> 00:34:47,719
three-wheeler here.

799
00:34:47,719 --> 00:34:48,679
Think it was easy for us?

800
00:34:49,239 --> 00:34:50,400
What car broke down?

801
00:34:50,760 --> 00:34:52,440
You just got a little money and had to show off.

802
00:34:52,599 --> 00:34:54,320
That siren ride I got this time

803
00:34:54,559 --> 00:34:55,440
was way better than yours.

804
00:34:55,639 --> 00:34:56,599
In that thing, you close your eyes,

805
00:34:56,719 --> 00:34:57,280
stretch out your legs,

806
00:34:57,360 --> 00:34:58,599
pure bliss, I'm telling you.

807
00:34:59,159 --> 00:35:00,400
What's so great about having a car?

808
00:35:01,119 --> 00:35:02,400
Then why didn't you just die?

809
00:35:04,440 --> 00:35:05,880
You barely recover and you're already showing off?

810
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:07,840
Why don't you just drop dead, then?

811
00:35:10,199 --> 00:35:11,360
Don't get smart with me, I'm telling you.

812
00:35:12,800 --> 00:35:13,800
The day I catch that punk,

813
00:35:13,840 --> 00:35:15,559
I'll slap him twice across the face first.

814
00:35:15,559 --> 00:35:16,119
I'm telling you,

815
00:35:16,960 --> 00:35:18,199
he did such a half-assed job!

816
00:35:19,199 --> 00:35:19,960
If he'd put a little more muscle into it,

817
00:35:19,960 --> 00:35:21,480
hit me a couple more times, it'd be done!

818
00:35:21,559 --> 00:35:22,880
I'd have gone straight to join Cao Jun!

819
00:35:23,559 --> 00:35:24,840
All right, all right, all right.

820
00:35:24,960 --> 00:35:25,599
Stop showing off.

821
00:35:26,280 --> 00:35:27,199
Count your blessings.

822
00:35:28,280 --> 00:35:30,079
Chunyan has been looking after you.

823
00:35:30,400 --> 00:35:31,000
Right?

824
00:35:32,199 --> 00:35:33,000
You just

825
00:35:33,239 --> 00:35:34,320
focus on recovering

826
00:35:35,840 --> 00:35:37,559
and cooperate with the police.

827
00:35:38,440 --> 00:35:39,400
Let's try our best

828
00:35:39,800 --> 00:35:41,360
to catch that bastard soon.

829
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:42,840
That's what really counts,

830
00:35:45,119 --> 00:35:45,639
right?

831
00:35:52,960 --> 00:35:53,480
Alright, then.

832
00:35:55,039 --> 00:35:55,599
We're taking off.

833
00:35:55,599 --> 00:35:56,159
Let's roll.

834
00:35:56,840 --> 00:35:57,519
Leaving already?

835
00:36:04,239 --> 00:36:04,920
Hold this for me.

836
00:36:08,960 --> 00:36:10,679
Didn't knock you stupid, did he?

837
00:36:13,039 --> 00:36:13,719
Look at you.

838
00:36:13,719 --> 00:36:14,800
You didn't have to bring anything,

839
00:36:15,079 --> 00:36:15,840
buying food to nurse me up.

840
00:36:16,119 --> 00:36:16,760
What about you two?

841
00:36:16,760 --> 00:36:17,840
Did you two come empty-handed?

842
00:36:19,199 --> 00:36:20,480
I'll stew an old hen for you later

843
00:36:21,360 --> 00:36:22,280
to build your strength back up.

844
00:36:23,559 --> 00:36:24,119
We're off.

845
00:36:26,239 --> 00:36:27,199
Thanks, Haipeng.

846
00:36:27,599 --> 00:36:28,840
It barely cost anything.

847
00:36:32,199 --> 00:36:32,760
Fasten it over here.

848
00:36:32,920 --> 00:36:33,599
It won't buckle.

849
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:34,679
Drive safe!

850
00:36:43,320 --> 00:36:46,280
If it were back in the day, that money...

851
00:36:50,760 --> 00:36:51,559
Exactly.

852
00:36:52,400 --> 00:36:54,360
She promised me she'd go to the auction.

853
00:36:55,039 --> 00:36:56,679
So how did she freeze to death?

854
00:37:03,519 --> 00:37:05,559
What happened to Xuemei...

855
00:37:07,679 --> 00:37:08,440
...it's fishy.

856
00:37:11,519 --> 00:37:12,000
Old Chen,

857
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:13,039
what—what are you getting at?

858
00:37:20,400 --> 00:37:21,800
Someone from the factory office,

859
00:37:22,559 --> 00:37:24,840
one of Ma Guowen's people, told me...

860
00:37:25,480 --> 00:37:26,320
...that yesterday,

861
00:37:28,559 --> 00:37:30,840
Ma Guowen and Xuemei...

862
00:37:31,400 --> 00:37:33,480
...shut the door in a private room

863
00:37:34,559 --> 00:37:35,679
and whispered for ages.

864
00:37:37,440 --> 00:37:38,360
And after that,

865
00:37:38,880 --> 00:37:40,000
Xuemei just left.

866
00:37:41,480 --> 00:37:42,920
The moment the auction started,

867
00:37:44,880 --> 00:37:45,760
she walked out.

868
00:37:46,280 --> 00:37:46,880
Then...

869
00:37:48,960 --> 00:37:49,440
what are you saying?

870
00:37:49,480 --> 00:37:51,320
Liu Xuemei sold us out?

871
00:37:51,320 --> 00:37:52,280
She's a traitor?

872
00:37:53,440 --> 00:37:54,400
I never said that.

873
00:37:54,679 --> 00:37:55,360
That's what you're implying!

874
00:37:55,800 --> 00:37:56,440
That's impossible!

875
00:37:59,800 --> 00:38:01,719
We were all locked inside the factory then.

876
00:38:02,559 --> 00:38:04,480
Xuemei was called over at the last minute, too.

877
00:38:04,480 --> 00:38:05,760
How could she be a traitor?

878
00:38:06,360 --> 00:38:06,960
Why couldn't she be?

879
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:08,159
She went into that private room!

880
00:38:09,119 --> 00:38:09,559
So what?

881
00:38:09,559 --> 00:38:10,400
Going into a private room makes her a traitor?

882
00:38:10,400 --> 00:38:10,960
That's enough!

883
00:38:11,280 --> 00:38:12,039
She's already dead.

884
00:38:12,880 --> 00:38:13,639
Drop it, both of you.

885
00:38:20,039 --> 00:38:21,239
Today, Ma Guowen...

886
00:38:21,360 --> 00:38:22,440
held meetings with every workshop,

887
00:38:23,760 --> 00:38:24,679
and said only one thing.

888
00:38:26,719 --> 00:38:27,360
What's that?

889
00:38:28,760 --> 00:38:29,480
Catch the ringleaders.

890
00:38:37,159 --> 00:38:38,639
What's that mean? Go ahead and arrest me!

891
00:38:39,840 --> 00:38:40,280
Come arrest me!

892
00:38:40,320 --> 00:38:40,840
Tie me up!

893
00:38:41,039 --> 00:38:41,599
Come on, take me, take me!

894
00:38:41,599 --> 00:38:42,440
Turn me in! What's it to you anyway?

895
00:38:42,440 --> 00:38:43,280
Come on, come on. Enough, cut it out.

896
00:38:43,280 --> 00:38:43,840
Come on!

897
00:38:44,360 --> 00:38:45,039
You always stick your neck out for everything.

898
00:38:45,079 --> 00:38:45,719
What do you mean by that?

899
00:38:47,079 --> 00:38:48,280
You've got nothing to worry about.

900
00:38:49,360 --> 00:38:50,119
You're a bachelor.

901
00:38:50,360 --> 00:38:50,960
Right?

902
00:38:51,400 --> 00:38:52,000
But think about it.

903
00:38:52,039 --> 00:38:53,559
There are so many people on that list.

904
00:38:54,679 --> 00:38:56,320
Everyone has a family to support.

905
00:38:56,559 --> 00:38:57,440
Right, exactly.

906
00:38:58,239 --> 00:38:59,480
Old Chen makes a good point.

907
00:39:00,440 --> 00:39:01,360
I think regarding this matter,

908
00:39:01,719 --> 00:39:03,480
we absolutely can't let Ma Guowen find out

909
00:39:03,559 --> 00:39:04,800
about our list.

910
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:05,679
Right, exactly.

911
00:39:05,880 --> 00:39:06,480
Now,

912
00:39:06,519 --> 00:39:07,599
Xiao Tu, keep it safe.

913
00:39:07,599 --> 00:39:09,000
We have to keep it well hidden.

914
00:39:09,679 --> 00:39:11,239
But now another problem has come up.

915
00:39:11,239 --> 00:39:11,800
What problem?

916
00:39:11,880 --> 00:39:13,440
We didn't get our factory back,

917
00:39:13,920 --> 00:39:15,480
and we haven't gotten our money back either.

918
00:39:15,639 --> 00:39:16,840
Rest easy.

919
00:39:16,840 --> 00:39:18,199
The money is at the auction house.

920
00:39:18,559 --> 00:39:19,800
I know it's at the auction house.

921
00:39:20,159 --> 00:39:21,599
But we can't just leave it sitting there.

922
00:39:21,719 --> 00:39:23,559
Having it in our own hands would give us peace of mind.

923
00:39:24,039 --> 00:39:24,760
That's a lot of money.

924
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:26,400
Right, we have to get it back.

925
00:39:26,800 --> 00:39:27,159
Exactly.

926
00:39:27,239 --> 00:39:27,800
Just think about it.

927
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:29,320
We're only about a hundred people.

928
00:39:29,320 --> 00:39:30,400
How hard was it to scrape together that 500,000?

929
00:39:30,519 --> 00:39:31,000
It's a huge sum.

930
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:31,320
Isn't it?

931
00:39:31,320 --> 00:39:31,719
Right.

932
00:39:32,639 --> 00:39:33,119
Chief Engineer Chen,

933
00:39:33,599 --> 00:39:34,480
how much did you drop with one wave of your hand?

934
00:39:34,559 --> 00:39:35,119
Fifty thousand.

935
00:39:35,239 --> 00:39:35,760
How much did you put in,

936
00:39:35,760 --> 00:39:36,119
Old Cao?

937
00:39:36,119 --> 00:39:36,480
Four thousand.

938
00:39:36,480 --> 00:39:37,280
My entire life savings went into that.

939
00:39:37,280 --> 00:39:37,960
You see?

940
00:39:38,360 --> 00:39:39,119
Normally speaking,

941
00:39:39,239 --> 00:39:39,559
Yeah.

942
00:39:39,599 --> 00:39:41,360
Xuemei handled the paperwork.

943
00:39:41,400 --> 00:39:41,800
Yeah.

944
00:39:41,880 --> 00:39:42,519
So to withdraw the money,

945
00:39:42,519 --> 00:39:43,280
Xuemei has to be the one to do it.

946
00:39:43,360 --> 00:39:43,719
That's right.

947
00:39:43,719 --> 00:39:44,559
But right now, she's...

948
00:39:44,599 --> 00:39:45,800
gone, isn't she?

949
00:39:45,920 --> 00:39:47,159
We can't just keep waiting around.

950
00:39:47,239 --> 00:39:48,760
I was thinking, shouldn't we find someone

951
00:39:48,800 --> 00:39:50,000
to go ask at the auction house?

952
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:50,400
Yeah, right.

953
00:39:50,400 --> 00:39:50,920
I'll go.

954
00:39:51,719 --> 00:39:52,360
Let me go.

955
00:39:52,840 --> 00:39:53,400
You can't.

956
00:39:54,360 --> 00:39:54,880
Why not?

957
00:39:55,159 --> 00:39:56,360
You'll drag the rest of us into it.

958
00:39:56,639 --> 00:39:57,239
Right, exactly.

959
00:39:57,519 --> 00:39:58,440
You can't go.

960
00:39:59,320 --> 00:40:00,960
We can't pick someone from our circle.

961
00:40:01,039 --> 00:40:01,920
We have to find someone

962
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:04,159
who has nothing to do with our circle.

963
00:40:20,280 --> 00:40:21,880
You don't actually...

964
00:40:22,360 --> 00:40:23,840
want me to go, do you?

965
00:40:24,800 --> 00:40:25,480
Exactly.

966
00:40:26,159 --> 00:40:27,760
Leshui isn't in our circle,

967
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:28,800
so she's the best fit.

968
00:40:28,880 --> 00:40:29,119
Yeah.

969
00:40:29,119 --> 00:40:30,119
No, no, no.

970
00:40:30,280 --> 00:40:30,719
No way.

971
00:40:30,960 --> 00:40:31,519
Look...

972
00:40:31,920 --> 00:40:32,519
Reporter Shen,

973
00:40:32,559 --> 00:40:33,239
no offense meant,

974
00:40:33,239 --> 00:40:34,320
but let me speak my mind.

975
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:38,039
Back when we discussed this,

976
00:40:38,320 --> 00:40:39,400
wasn't it to keep it from Ma Guowen?

977
00:40:39,480 --> 00:40:40,960
Just a few of us here in private,

978
00:40:40,960 --> 00:40:42,000
without any outsiders around?

979
00:40:42,280 --> 00:40:43,440
So how did Ma Guowen find out later?

980
00:40:43,760 --> 00:40:44,840
Back then, wasn't the only outsider...

981
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:46,280
her?

982
00:40:47,639 --> 00:40:48,000
Her!

983
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:48,719
What's that supposed to mean?

984
00:40:50,519 --> 00:40:52,199
What did Leshui do to you now?

985
00:40:53,800 --> 00:40:54,960
One minute you suspect this person,

986
00:40:54,960 --> 00:40:55,800
the next you suspect that person.

987
00:40:56,000 --> 00:40:56,639
What's your deal, Cao Jun?

988
00:40:56,639 --> 00:40:57,960
What are you trying to pull?

989
00:40:58,159 --> 00:40:58,840
I'm not pulling anything.

990
00:40:58,920 --> 00:40:59,320
Haipeng.

991
00:40:59,760 --> 00:41:00,039
Look,

992
00:41:00,039 --> 00:41:01,320
I know you two are dating,

993
00:41:01,719 --> 00:41:03,199
but hear me out.

994
00:41:03,199 --> 00:41:04,480
She's the only outsider here.

995
00:41:04,679 --> 00:41:06,519
What if she actually takes the money?

996
00:41:06,639 --> 00:41:06,960
You—

997
00:41:07,079 --> 00:41:07,920
Leaving the money in an outsider's hands...

998
00:41:07,920 --> 00:41:09,960
What does this have to do with us dating?

999
00:41:10,119 --> 00:41:10,519
Fine, fine, fine.

1000
00:41:10,519 --> 00:41:11,119
She... I...

1001
00:41:11,119 --> 00:41:11,519
Right, right, right.

1002
00:41:11,519 --> 00:41:12,079
You make a good point.

1003
00:41:12,440 --> 00:41:13,239
Then why don't you go?

1004
00:41:13,559 --> 00:41:14,119
Me? I...

1005
00:41:14,280 --> 00:41:15,199
How can I go?

1006
00:41:15,199 --> 00:41:15,880
Can I even go?

1007
00:41:16,039 --> 00:41:17,000
I'm just a driver.

1008
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:17,760
How am I supposed to go?

1009
00:41:17,920 --> 00:41:18,960
I don't even know

1010
00:41:18,960 --> 00:41:19,719
where the auction is being held.

1011
00:41:19,719 --> 00:41:20,199
How am I supposed to go?

1012
00:41:20,199 --> 00:41:20,920
I can't go.

1013
00:41:21,519 --> 00:41:22,480
Then that settles it.

1014
00:41:29,960 --> 00:41:31,280
This is an unusual situation.

1015
00:41:32,239 --> 00:41:33,360
Everyone's anxious,

1016
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:36,079
so it's natural you'd suspect me.

1017
00:41:37,880 --> 00:41:39,079
But right now, only I

1018
00:41:39,519 --> 00:41:41,800
can go ask the auction house for you all.

1019
00:41:42,039 --> 00:41:42,880
Leshui, you're not going.

1020
00:41:44,159 --> 00:41:45,320
They don't even trust you.

1021
00:41:45,840 --> 00:41:46,599
Why bother going?

1022
00:41:47,920 --> 00:41:48,719
Stay out of this.

1023
00:41:53,280 --> 00:41:53,800
How about this?

1024
00:41:54,960 --> 00:41:55,920
You all come with me.

1025
00:41:56,159 --> 00:41:57,280
Keep watch outside,

1026
00:41:58,519 --> 00:41:59,440
and I'll go in alone.

1027
00:42:00,039 --> 00:42:00,960
When registering names,

1028
00:42:01,039 --> 00:42:02,440
I'll only put down mine.

1029
00:42:03,280 --> 00:42:04,440
You won't be exposed.

1030
00:42:24,800 --> 00:42:25,360
Hello.

1031
00:42:25,559 --> 00:42:26,239
How can I help you?

1032
00:42:26,559 --> 00:42:27,039
Hello.

1033
00:42:27,480 --> 00:42:28,920
I'm here to retrieve a deposit.

1034
00:42:29,880 --> 00:42:30,920
On the 30th of last month,

1035
00:42:30,920 --> 00:42:31,760
from Lapi Brewery,

1036
00:42:32,039 --> 00:42:33,760
our representative, Liu Xuemei,

1037
00:42:34,239 --> 00:42:35,719
paid 500,000

1038
00:42:35,719 --> 00:42:37,440
as an auction deposit.

1039
00:42:37,760 --> 00:42:38,960
You should have a record of it here.

1040
00:42:39,079 --> 00:42:39,679
All right.

1041
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:42,119
Here's the thing.

1042
00:42:42,880 --> 00:42:44,480
She unfortunately passed away.

1043
00:42:45,280 --> 00:42:46,199
But this money

1044
00:42:46,239 --> 00:42:48,519
was pooled by many of us workers.

1045
00:42:49,000 --> 00:42:50,400
In this situation,

1046
00:42:50,559 --> 00:42:53,239
how can we get this money back?

1047
00:42:53,880 --> 00:42:54,599
Here's how it works.

1048
00:42:54,800 --> 00:42:55,599
For pooled funds,

1049
00:42:55,679 --> 00:42:57,440
all contributors must give authorization

1050
00:42:57,440 --> 00:42:58,199
to make a withdrawal.

1051
00:42:58,599 --> 00:42:59,280
I'm sorry.

1052
00:42:59,440 --> 00:43:00,880
Everyone?

1053
00:43:01,920 --> 00:43:03,960
Does every single person have to sign?

1054
00:43:04,199 --> 00:43:04,679
Yes.

1055
00:43:21,159 --> 00:43:22,639
Liu Xuemei's death—

1056
00:43:22,880 --> 00:43:24,519
was it tied to Gao Wusong,

1057
00:43:25,360 --> 00:43:26,400
or

1058
00:43:27,320 --> 00:43:29,000
were they murdered together?

1059
00:43:31,559 --> 00:43:32,599
Maybe this whole thing

1060
00:43:32,800 --> 00:43:34,159
got back to people at the brewery,

1061
00:43:34,800 --> 00:43:35,519
so

1062
00:43:36,039 --> 00:43:38,559
you're burying the truth for your father.

1063
00:43:39,239 --> 00:43:39,960
That's why

1064
00:43:40,880 --> 00:43:42,679
you stole my tape.
